# MAGIC -- Grain: one row per ORIGINAL failure incident (not per poll, not per retry
# MAGIC -- attempt separately). Retries update the same row via latest_run_id and
# MAGIC -- retry_count, so max-retry limits apply correctly per failure chain.
# MAGIC --
# MAGIC -- status values (state machine):
# MAGIC --   detected            -> failure found, not yet classified
# MAGIC --   classified          -> AI has classified it (transient/permanent/unknown)
# MAGIC --   retry_scheduled      -> decided to retry, waiting for scheduled time
# MAGIC --   retried              -> retry was triggered, new run in progress
# MAGIC --   resolved             -> a newer run of this job succeeded, no more action
# MAGIC --   permanent_no_action  -> classified permanent, no retry taken
# MAGIC --   max_retries_reached  -> exhausted retry attempts, escalate to human
